1
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,390
you stop?

2
00:00:57,319 --> 00:00:58,780
We'll go there to the place

3
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:05,100
We'll go there to the place Dreaming on!

4
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,277
I'm so dumb, I'm so dumb.

5
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,242
I'm going to fight, I'm so dumb.

6
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:16,720
I'm loving my self-serve.

7
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,877
I'll be dreaming on!

8
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:24,040
Whoa-oh!

9
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,220
Whoa-oh!

10
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:30,020
Whoa! Whoa-oh!

11
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,500
Really kept me waiting!

12
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:01,300
Yo-ho!

13
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:06,510
TJ!

14
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:15,340
Everyone, from this day forward,
I'm officially a Straw Hat!

15
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:21,260
We were all so worried about you!

16
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:22,790
Mr.

17
00:02:22,873 --> 00:02:25,320
T, the boss is back!

18
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,340
I'm relieved as well.

19
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,718
Seems you've had quite the struggle.

20
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,732
It's wild we have a former
warlord of the sea on our crew.

21
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:38,860
You're gonna kick so much ass.

22
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:41,940
I'm so glad he's all right.

23
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:50,120
Nami, could you please don't
know the intimacy of that hug?

24
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:58,720
I was really worried about you, man.

25
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:01,300
It took a while. My apologies.

26
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:06,557
Some of the sun pirates were wounded,
so I had to tend to them first.

27
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:09,816
Then they threw me a big
send-off for old time's sake.

28
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,616
Forgive me, Captain.

29
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:14,160
But you know how it is.

30
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,240
Everyone, thank you for having me.

31
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:21,260
And once again, I shall do my best.

32
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,887
You won't believe this
guy's steering skills.

33
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:29,477
Jinbei, you gotta show off!

34
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,997
He even used the Sunny
like a big surfboard.

35
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,120
Freakin' sweet!

36
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:35,217
It's about time.

37
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:38,917
We finally got a guy who can make
full use of the ship of dreams.

38
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,237
Let's do this!

39
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,900
Time for a toast, right?

40
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,100
Oh yeah!

41
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,140
Now let's drink!

42
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:52,700
Hold up a second We don't have
any alcohol on hand, though.

43
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:54,290
Wrong.

44
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,080
I can smell some booze in the air.

45
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,617
Then where the hell is it?

46
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:00,700
Right over there.

47
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,550
Hey!

48
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:07,960
Sir Luffy!

49
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:10,157
If you have a moment,

50
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:14,652
I would like to discuss our next course
of action once we reach the island.

51
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,860
You hear me?

52
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:18,000
Please, make your way over to us.

53
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,240
Sir Luffy!

54
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:21,940
You're lying your ass off.

55
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:23,597
All I can smell is the ocean.

56
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,200
I am NOT a liar!

57
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:29,780
I smell food over that way!

58
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,280
Please, Sir Luffy!

59
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,380
Give it up.

60
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,657
There's no point in trying
to reason with them.

61
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,622
They're not gonna listen to you.

62
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:41,601
Besides, you bums are on my ship.

63
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:44,544
If you want to talk
strategy, take it elsewhere.

64
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:55,900
Please excuse my tardiness.

65
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:58,720
I wish to be briefed on your strategy.

66
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,160
Oh-ho!

67
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,460
Sir Full Power Cecilion! Duke Dogstorm,

68
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:12,277
I know that Ugarra will be fighting
as a retainer for the Kozuki clan.

69
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:16,680
Therefore, allow me to lead the big
forces in your stead, sir. Splendid.

70
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:18,001
Thank you, Karoo.

71
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:19,840
Allow me as well.

72
00:05:20,700 --> 00:05:23,440
It would be my humble honor to assist you.

73
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:25,996
I will take command over the samurai.

74
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:32,200
Boss Yoguro, it's you.

75
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,317
You must forgive my lengthy disappearance.

76
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,165
I know that you have suffered.

77
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:38,400
I am delighted to see you as well.

78
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,597
Now, before we reach our destination,

79
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:43,137
let's work out the details
of our plan, shall we?

80
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:45,017
I trust you have everything in order?

81
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:45,930
Of course!

82
00:05:46,013 --> 00:05:46,843
Those bastards.

83
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:50,434
Look at them making themselves
right at home on my deck.

84
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:56,060
Gentlemen, I only have time to
explain this plan once, so heed well.

85
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,864
Let's take a glance at the map.

86
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:02,656
Onigashima is a remote island
surrounded by mountains.

87
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:08,865
Even if you attempt to proceed by boat,
the steep mountainside will bar your way.

88
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,560
It's impenetrable!

89
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:14,000
There is but a single
entrance to the entire island,

90
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,592
and that would be through the front gate.

91
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:20,369
The Giant Skull is a rock
formation surrounded by mountains,

92
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:22,540
with Kaido's castle hidden inside.

93
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:25,377
Referencing the blueprints
that we had stolen,

94
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:29,460
there is a rear entrance located
on the opposite side of the island.

95
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:30,770
Understand?

96
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:34,784
Our best bet is to avoid the
heavily guarded front gate entirely.

97
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:35,850
Therefore,

98
00:06:35,933 --> 00:06:37,457
we shall separate into two groups,

99
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:40,977
take the mountain paths to the left
and right, then infiltrate from behind.

100
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:45,600
Kaido will be intoxicated after the
festivities, so we'll make it quick.

101
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:47,508
It'll be a surprise attack.

102
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:48,840
We cannot fail!

103
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:53,820
That's rather impressive.

104
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:58,357
That was the decoy plan you set in
Kanjuro's presence to deceive him, right?

105
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:00,937
Though the details are
a bit hastily crafted,

106
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:04,373
it will surely serve its
purpose and throw off the enemy.

107
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,670
Decoy?

108
00:07:05,753 --> 00:07:08,100
Now, what is the real strategy?

109
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:13,740
He's over-evaluating again.

110
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,911
Firstly, you have to assume
the enemy is aware of the raid.

111
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:22,399
And they'll actively seek out the
Akazaya Samurai before anyone else.

112
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,640
They'll also be looking for me.

113
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:31,338
Since we're all captains, that goes
for Straw Hat and Eustass as well.

114
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,000
Indeed, that is true.

115
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:37,477
Honestly, it won't matter what
kind of plan you slap together.

116
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:40,384
We're dealing with two
Carrot idiots as allies.

117
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:42,277
We'll charge straight in no matter what.

118
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,190
No!

119
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:49,291
But if we use them as decoys,
we can salvage the operation.

120
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:51,875
Lucky for us, they can hold their own.

121
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,777
Once Kaido finds out he's been invaded,

122
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:57,657
he's going to send out everything
he's got to stop those two dumbasses.

123
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:58,840
I understand now!

124
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:02,397
So when our pirate friends undoubtedly
run straight for the entrance,

125
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:05,577
the guards will leave the rest
of the palace relatively clear!

126
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:06,490
Right.

127
00:08:06,573 --> 00:08:10,439
We'll use that opportunity to proceed
down the side paths as planned.

128
00:08:11,540 --> 00:08:14,834
However, that too is a diversion
to protect the samurai.

129
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:19,387
We're prepared for anything.

130
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:21,874
Even if we need to sacrifice ourselves,

131
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:25,617
the Akazaya samurai must make
it to the battle against Kaido.

132
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:27,317
That's the only thing that matters.

133
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,224
I agree, but how will you
gotta get them inside?

134
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,340
They'll go by water.

135
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,396
Forgetting a detail?

136
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,597
Won't the whirlpools be an issue for us?

137
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,037
That part's already covered.

138
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,591
There's no need to worry.

139
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:43,104
We're going to use the
Polar Tang, my submarine.

140
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:48,724
By taking it around the back of the island,
we'll avoid the whirlpools altogether.

141
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:50,180
Then I'm up.

142
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:55,013
I'll use my room ability to
send you all onto the island.

143
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,920
Sir Law, thank you.

144
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:01,992
But there's one concern.

145
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:06,097
I feel that at the very least, I
must be there to lead the troops.

146
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:07,180
You have a point.

147
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:10,017
Then we should send
one of us on each path.

148
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:13,897
I will take the one side of the
mountain, and you can take the other.

149
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:19,560
What say you? Raizo? Kawamatsu?
Dogstorm? Kikunojo? Ashura?

150
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,380
I agree.

151
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:25,157
In the meantime, the rest of
us will all stick together.

152
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:28,577
We'll make sure to save our full
strength for the fight against Kaido.

153
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:29,490
Very good.

154
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,420
Just as I planned it.

155
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:33,880
We'll go with this strategy.

156
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:35,700
Very clever, Keen.

157
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:37,540
Incredible plan.

158
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:39,700
Yeah, Keen.

159
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,300
See the Dorry Gate here?

160
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:51,137
That's the first hindrance we'll
face when we enter Onigashima.

161
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,680
How serious is this?

162
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,337
Are there guards involved?

163
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:55,940
Yes, and that isn't all.

164
00:09:56,240 --> 00:10:00,181
It serves as both an entrance and
a small armed fortress for Kaido.

165
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:03,222
They should have plenty
of cannons to fire at us.

166
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,857
Keep in mind, today is the fire festival.

167
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:11,937
More beast pirates than usual
will be waiting on Onigashima.

168
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:14,077
I see, so proceed cautiously.

169
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,477
We don't know how many
of them are expecting us.

170
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:18,097
I suggest we stick together.

171
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:20,097
That way if we're found,
we still have a chance.

172
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:21,117
This sounds risky.

173
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,437
No matter the case.

174
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:25,120
We must inform our allies of this at once.

175
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:30,670
Hey.

176
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:34,026
Where in the hell did
the Straw Hat's boat go?

177
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:35,750
No!

178
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,500
Oh no, Sir Luffy!

179
00:10:39,660 --> 00:10:41,337
Please don't tell me that was them!

180
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,397
Quickly, sir-law!

181
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:43,657
Send your vessel that way!

182
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:45,757
They must be in dire need of assistance!

183
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,800
All right, now, Com-Cum!

184
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:50,720
Up there!

185
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,860
Don't let them get any closer! Fire!

186
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:03,940
Blast them away! Take it!

187
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,940
Oh, God!

188
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:08,770
I'm not there!

189
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,560
Don't go pistol!

190
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:28,620
It's over for you!

191
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:46,320
Two-sword style.

192
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,480
Now, Hawkwave!

193
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:14,240
It seems you have me surrounded.

194
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:16,400
Time to take him out!

195
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,580
Not so solid.

196
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:34,440
Swallow Thunder!

197
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:38,770
Oh!

198
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:48,820
Now, me who flew, gigantesca model!

199
00:12:58,940 --> 00:12:59,770
And stomp!

200
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:24,460
My sweet ramen.

201
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:25,760
Hey, suit guy!

202
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,717
Think you can just light
a cigarette mid-fight?

203
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,630
Ah!

204
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:31,080
Ah! Ah!

205
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:35,170
Flanchez!

206
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:40,957
Yeah!

207
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:41,960
Franky!

208
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,100
Fucking!

209
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:47,820
Super!

210
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:56,460
I think they're doing just
fine without our help. Agreed?

211
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:06,857
All right, decent fighting, man.

212
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:07,940
It was all right.

213
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:11,100
Yes, acceptable. Good job,
troops. Adequate work.

214
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:14,065
Why'd you guys just wait
on the sidelines, huh?

215
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:19,380
The Dorry gate guards, they
were all knocked out. Oh, wow.

216
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:21,052
That's a lot of weapons.

217
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,247
Imagine if we'd fought them.

218
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:27,275
Our number of troops would
have dwindled down for sure.

219
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:30,620
Then that means we can
all sail forth together.

220
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:36,380
To Onigashima!

221
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:00,100
That was a ton of good
alcohol you just wasted!

222
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:18,420
Oh, Lord Archie, you'll
never catch up to me!

223
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:20,540
I won't?

224
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:22,600
Well, here I come, my pretty!

225
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,071
Seems like someone's in a good mood today.

226
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:33,437
I like it when you're happy, Mr. Shogun.

227
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:34,460
It's adorable!

228
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:37,197
I bet something really
nice happened to you.

229
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:39,017
What clever girls you all are!

230
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,100
How did you know?

231
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:42,000
Oh boy, tell us!

232
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,720
Well, it's a most splendid day.

233
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:48,977
There was some trash in my way and
it's finally been disposed of, you see.

234
00:15:49,060 --> 00:15:52,800
Now that garbage is finally in
the ground where it belongs.

235
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:57,517
So you're extra happy today because
somebody took the garbage out?

236
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:00,040
The Shogun is such a weirdo sometimes!

237
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:04,940
Do you lovely ladies
really find it that odd?

238
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:06,770
Obviously!

239
00:16:06,853 --> 00:16:09,440
But it's cute in a quirky way! Yeah!

240
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:17,560
As the shogun of Wano, I declare that
it is now a lord to come to daddy!

241
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,500
Which of you dare to defy my orders?

242
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:26,077
You, where the hell is my Ashiruko?

243
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:27,984
I apologize for the delay, sir.

244
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:30,937
We'll bring it to you right
after we deliver Big Mom's order.

245
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:31,980
Big Mom?

246
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,640
Why does she get to skip the line?

247
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:38,757
Did you forget there's gonna be a
performance for the banquet tonight?

248
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:40,252
I'm a little foggy here.

249
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:42,477
Why don't you remind me who's the star?

250
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:45,384
The man's name is right
on the tip of my tongue.

251
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:46,690
Queen!

252
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,390
Yeah!

253
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:49,660
Damn right it's me!

254
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:52,977
And which lead performer's
got the pipes and the talent?

255
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:53,890
Queen!

256
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,320
That's for sure.

257
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:56,580
Can you dig it?

258
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:57,980
So feed me.

259
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:59,886
I can't lose any more weight.

260
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:02,580
The ladies will go crazy.

261
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:09,720
Wipe that stupid grin off
your face and get moving!

262
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:15,540
The party's in full swing, and
everyone's having a great time. Agreed.

263
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:18,737
And I'm really looking forward
to the big show tonight, sir.

264
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:21,120
Do we know if he's joining us? Who?

265
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:23,040
I'm talking about my son.

266
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:24,755
He needs to be there!

267
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:25,880
It's the banquet!

268
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:27,198
I'll find him, sir!

269
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:29,150
Commander!

270
00:17:29,233 --> 00:17:32,220
All six members of the Toby
Rope have just arrived!

271
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:33,400
Are you ready?

272
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:35,193
They're here to see me.

273
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:37,577
I might as well introduce them to Lin-Lin.

274
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,895
Where the hell is the old bag, anyway?

275
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,820
It's not a good time, sir.

276
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:45,760
Big Mom is changing into her
kimono at this moment. What?

277
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:47,721
Commander Kaido!

278
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:49,660
The Toby Rope are outside.

279
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:51,900
Bring them to me!

280
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,350
Ugh!

281
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:36,220
I don't know.

282
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:06,117
The Brachio of the tiptoes like a mofo,

283
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,457
no need to be vague, you
know him as the plague!

284
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:11,440
Coming to you in widescreen!

285
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:19,160
It's Conney!

286
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:25,860
I keep you waiting!

287
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,840
Give it up, give it up!

288
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:31,100
You ready to kick off the Golden Festival?

289
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,160
It's time to party!

290
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:48,360
Not gonna lose no weight,
just more to appreciate.

291
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:52,200
I got enough fans attracted to my funk!

292
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,350
Yeah!

293
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,130
Yeah!

294
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:03,540
I look round as a ball, but
all of this is muscle, y 'all!

295
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:06,780
These bomb-ass moves of
mine are powered by my...

296
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:10,140
Y 'all are right on the gotcha ball!

297
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:13,840
Let me hear you scream!

298
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,260
Now you know how this goes!

299
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:20,700
I'ma do a little roll call, y 'all!

300
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,136
Now make some noise!

301
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:29,697
It's your time, not a moment later What
you say, are you sick of waiting, waiters?

302
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:30,610
Yeah!

303
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:34,977
You're down to the dumps,
but life is your treasure.

304
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:36,884
Come on, laugh it at pleasures!

305
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:42,717
Bless with the gift of smiles and clothes.

306
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:44,580
Gifters, let it all out!

307
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:50,417
The headliners know they're
the cream of the crop.

308
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,794
Let me hear your call out from the top!

309
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:58,257
Last but not least, top six of the face.

310
00:20:58,340 --> 00:21:00,137
Strong and dangerous like my slow.

311
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:03,220
Give it up, y 'all, for Z-Toby-Rabba!

312
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:11,680
Ah, psych!

313
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:14,640
Those pretentious asses never respond.

314
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,901
They stayed under how I can lose.

315
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:19,697
Now where my monsters at?

316
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:21,140
No, let's go!

317
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:30,620
You hearing this shit show?

318
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:32,080
What do I care?

319
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,620
Orochi's forces, pick it up!

320
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:37,880
Gonna need the Mimawari
Koby to raise the roof!

321
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:41,080
No, the only one but you!

322
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,660
But wait, there's more!

323
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:46,017
I hear we have some
special guests tonight.

324
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:48,100
Y 'all ready for a family reunion?

325
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:51,520
Big Mom's kids are on the way!

326
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:58,140
Queen won't shut his big fat face.

327
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:01,240
Did you hear him call us a bunch of asses?

328
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:02,980
He's ever, ever so awful!

329
00:22:03,260 --> 00:22:05,040
So is that your new thing now?

330
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:07,340
Trying to sound like a fancy lady?

331
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:09,365
Give it up, it's embarrassing.

332
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:11,797
Aw, don't be such a booger, Papa!

333
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,710
Don't call me that!

334
00:22:12,793 --> 00:22:14,132
It's ever, ever so lame!

335
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:19,077
Suppose old queen happened
to drop dead tonight,

336
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:21,637
there'd be a lead performer vacancy.

337
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:23,517
Who would it go to?

338
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,117
Answer him, Drake!

339
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:27,729
You think you're the
most qualified, right?

340
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:31,417
I'm not interested in
becoming a lead performer.

341
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:32,597
Don't be stupid!

342
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,797
Oh, you dropping out of the race?

343
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:37,017
Because that would work
out perfectly for me.

344
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:39,877
Much obliged, and what about you?

345
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:42,220
Pay, pay, you passing? Huh?

346
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:45,077
I don't think you got
the chops since you let

347
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:48,120
Sobermask get away without
so much as a scratch.

348
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:50,700
You take that back!

349
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:56,660
If you insult my sweet Papa one more time,
I'll snap you like a twig - Stop it, sis!

350
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:57,710
Fine!

351
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,442
You don't get to boss me around!

352
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:00,410
Calm down!

353
00:23:00,493 --> 00:23:02,751
You think you can tell me what to do, huh?

354
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:05,880
Hey, that's enough
screeching, you damn crats.

355
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:08,298
I find their antics rather charming.

356
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:12,480
I love it when Ellie throws a tantrum.

357
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:14,160
She's out for blood.

358
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:19,857
So are we just waiting around, or
did they call us here for a reason?

359
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:21,220
The usual, I'm sure.

360
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:23,108
We were told it was urgent.

361
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:24,460
Kaido's orders.

362
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,960
Take a guess what he wants.

363
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:30,260
So it's dysfunctional family junk again?

364
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:39,140
Is Kaido stupid or something?

365
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:41,555
Don't trash talk the commander, idiot!

366
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:48,820
Get him on! Over here!

367
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:50,940
We beat up some guys!

368
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,540
I was hoping we'd have more leeway.

369
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:59,020
Yo, Mosshead! Huh? Huh?

370
00:23:59,420 --> 00:24:01,420
Where the hell did that come from?

371
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:03,180
Didn't I tell you?

372
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,120
I know that smell anywhere.

373
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:08,360
He's like an animal. Hey! It's Freddy!

374
00:24:08,780 --> 00:24:10,440
Come on, you guys, hurry up!

375
00:24:11,180 --> 00:24:12,010
Coming!

376
00:24:13,180 --> 00:24:14,600
We've got a toast to me!

377
00:24:16,240 --> 00:24:17,070
Luffy!

378
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:19,837
Come on, we're going to drink
it all before you get here!

379
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:20,940
Or Zoro will.

380
00:24:21,180 --> 00:24:22,360
No, I won't!

381
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:23,840
I'm on my way!

382
00:24:24,540 --> 00:24:26,011
Here's one for you, boss.

383
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:28,340
Thank you, Godly.

384
00:24:28,940 --> 00:24:33,116
Raise a toast to Koby, the super
houndsman we've all been waiting for.

385
00:24:33,380 --> 00:24:36,560
Aw, if we had some more
time, I'd break out a song.

386
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:42,980
You know, exchanging sake cups
is usually a more solemn affair.

387
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:47,180
All right, get your cups
ready, guys. Cheers! Cheers!

388
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:57,360
Koby, we're so glad you came back our way.

389
00:24:58,140 --> 00:25:00,552
Thank you for your assistance, Sir Luffy.

390
00:25:01,060 --> 00:25:03,760
You have cleared our
first obstacle for us.

391
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:06,360
And now we go forward!

392
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:16,780
You see that?

393
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:18,377
Since when are they so excited?

394
00:25:18,460 --> 00:25:19,617
If I had to guess,

395
00:25:19,700 --> 00:25:23,137
seeing that fortress dismantled
must have boosted everyone's morale.

396
00:25:23,220 --> 00:25:26,277
Once we get to Onigashima, I bet
they're really gonna lead loose.

397
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:28,537
Hurry up and finish the toast already!

398
00:25:28,620 --> 00:25:31,149
We gotta get moving so
we can back them up!

399
00:25:35,420 --> 00:25:37,977
We must not let this
opportunity go to waste.

400
00:25:38,060 --> 00:25:39,648
Let's keep up the momentum.

401
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:40,950
Right.

402
00:25:41,033 --> 00:25:42,720
Our foes will never see us coming.

403
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:44,520
How lucky we are.

404
00:25:44,780 --> 00:25:47,660
The Straw Hats are quite
an asset. They are.

405
00:25:47,900 --> 00:25:50,740
My despair has been washed away at last.

406
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:54,195
Now we're carried on the
waves of hope that they bring.

407
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:57,960
To arms, loyal samurai!

408
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:00,620
Take a stand as a Kozuki warrior!

409
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,700
We shall lead you!

410
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:05,060
All ships to Onigashima!

411
00:26:11,860 --> 00:26:13,580
Our moment is now!

412
00:26:32,940 --> 00:26:34,520
What's going on with you?

413
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:38,430
Luffy.

414
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:40,457
Why are you being so weird?

415
00:26:40,540 --> 00:26:41,481
Drop the drinks.

416
00:26:42,840 --> 00:26:44,280
Save it for the samurai.

417
00:26:45,300 --> 00:26:47,300
The beast, the toast, everything.

418
00:26:49,220 --> 00:26:51,420
Let's do it after we beat Kaido.

419
00:26:52,460 --> 00:26:54,897
And we'll kick Uruji
and Big Mom's ass, too.

420
00:26:54,980 --> 00:27:01,440
Two, after all this is over, we can
have the biggest, best party ever!

421
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:04,280
Let's go win this thing!

422
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:12,217
You know, you're the one who wanted
to stop and have the stupid toast.

423
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:14,297
But sure, it changed
our plans last second.

424
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:15,210
That's right.

425
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:16,297
You tell him, Nami.

426
00:27:16,380 --> 00:27:17,210
Tell me what?

427
00:27:17,293 --> 00:27:18,897
I don't see why you guys are surprised.

428
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:19,917
He does what he wants.

429
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,588
There's no point in us
complaining about it.

430
00:27:22,940 --> 00:27:24,780
Hey, why are you nodding, too?

431
00:27:24,980 --> 00:27:27,156
It seems that the captain has spoken,

432
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:30,261
but how do you feel about
delaying the party boss?

433
00:27:32,660 --> 00:27:35,460
I'm pretty sure you
already know my answer!

434
00:27:37,800 --> 00:27:39,120
We're in!

435
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:46,760
All right!

436
00:27:47,020 --> 00:27:48,500
Let's get a move on!

437
00:27:48,820 --> 00:27:50,520
Follow those samurai!

438
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:52,900
I am captain!
